# ============================================================
# FEATURE: Evaluation Metrics – Signal Score
# Priority: CRITICAL
# ============================================================

## Why this feature is critical

Signal Score is the core trust metric for Sioona.
It measures how accurate our signal detection is based on human feedback.
Without reliable Signal Score, we cannot:

- Build trust with design partners
- Move from Shadow Mode to any autonomous actions
- Improve the detection system systematically
- Convert pilots into paying customers

This feature must be treated as high-priority, clean, and production-grade.

## Core Definition

**Pilot win metric (SoT):** human **keep-set** SignalScore on the Eval **week window** (`reviewed_at` / `?scoreFrom=`) ≥80% — see `.cursor/docs/PROJECT_STATE.md`. Empty week window → Reviewed 0 / **Insufficient Data**, never a labeled-fixture Go.

Signal types (only): `lead` | `retention` | `upsell`.

Feedback labels (only): `correct` | `incorrect` | `partially_correct`.

Keep-set SignalScore = correct / (correct + incorrect) among human-reviewed signals in the keep set for the selected week window (orphan Partner Demo rows excluded from the keep set, not deleted). Labeled precision/recall on fixtures is **not** the customer claim.

We also track:

- Per-signal-type breakdown (`lead`, `retention`, `upsell`)
- Basic support for Precision / Recall when labeled evaluation data is available (pack / CLI only)

## Strict Rules for this feature

### Data & Models

- Every prediction must be stored with: tenant_id, conversation_id, signal_type, confidence, summary, created_at
- Every human feedback must be stored with: signal_id, feedback (`correct` / `incorrect` / `partially_correct`), optional note, reviewed_by, reviewed_at
- Always keep multi-tenancy (tenant_id) on every table/query
- Never delete feedback data (it is valuable training signal)
- Signal Score + pending queue SoT: FastAPI + Neon (`backend/`) — do not invent a parallel score path

### Calculation Rules

- Signal Score must only be calculated from human-reviewed signals
- Pilot Eval uses keep-set + week window (not “all reviewed forever” as the go/no-go claim)
- Support filtering by: tenant, date range / week window, signal_type
- Keep the calculation simple and transparent
- Avoid over-engineering (no complex weighting in v1)

### API & Service Rules

- Prefer existing FastAPI services/endpoints for:
  - Recording a prediction
  - Recording human feedback
  - Calculating Signal Score
- All endpoints must be tenant-aware
- Do **not** rebuild Signal Score / week-window / keep-set features already shipped

### Code Quality

- Keep the code modular and easy to test
- Prefer simple, readable logic over clever abstractions
- Add basic docstrings
- Do not mix UI code with this feature
- Do not add autonomous actions or complex agent logic here

### What NOT to do in this feature

- Do not invent signal types (`retention_risk`, `churn_risk`, `fraud`, etc.)
- Do not use legacy feedback names (`accept` / `reject` / `wrong_reason`)
- Do not treat labeled P/R as the pilot go/no-go
- Do not implement full Precision/Recall pipelines unless explicitly asked
- Do not add complex ML evaluation frameworks
- Do not weaken multi-tenancy

## Implementation Preference

When asked to change this feature:

1. Read `.cursor/docs/PROJECT_STATE.md` + existing `backend/` score/feedback services first
2. Outline the files and data models if a real gap exists
3. Extend services/API only — do not rebuild
4. Keep everything focused only on Evaluation Metrics / Signal Score

## Success Criteria for this feature

- We can record model predictions
- Humans can mark signals as `correct` / `incorrect` / `partially_correct`
- We can calculate and return keep-set Signal Score (overall + per `lead` / `retention` / `upsell`) for a week window
- The system is multi-tenant safe
- The code is clean enough to extend later with Precision/Recall
